{
  "choices": [
    {
      "message": {
        "content": "{\n  \"chapter_id\": \"Ch4_Context\",\n  \"chapter_argument\": \"肠道微生物组对 ICI 疗效的调节作用具有高度情境依赖性，其预测价值受治疗方案时序、药物暴露窗口、宿主生理背景及肿瘤内在特征的多维修饰。解释临床关联异质性必须将微生物信号置于该调节变量框架下，而非寻求普适标志物。抗生素与 PPI 的负面影响依赖使用时窗与抗菌谱，饮食与年龄通过重塑基线菌群改变预测力，而肿瘤类型与分子亚型决定了微生物效应的可及性与方向。\",\n  \"units\": [\n    {\n      \"unit_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U01\",\n      \"focus\": \"治疗方案类型（单药/化疗联合/双免联合）与时序安排系统性修饰肠道微生物组的预测效力，特定菌属或代谢物仅在特定治疗背景下呈现稳定关联。\",\n      \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U01_P01\",\n          \"point\": \"化疗联合免疫与双免方案下微生物预测方向的异质性\",\n          \"development\": \"对比 P0585 中 NIC 与 PC 组 Prevotellaceae 及产丁酸菌的相反预后方向，论证联合化疗通过重塑 TME 淋巴细胞浸润模式，改变了肠道菌群信号向抗肿瘤免疫转化的阈值与路径。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供化疗 - 免疫联合与双免联合下同一菌属呈现相反预后方向的直接证据，支持治疗方案修饰预测力的核心论点。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0053\",\n              \"role\": \"例证\",\n              \"use\": \"阐明化疗联合双免方案如何覆盖基线微生物多样性的预测信号，论证治疗强度与组合模式是决定菌群标志物临床效用的关键情境变量。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U01_P02\",\n          \"point\": \"既往抗肿瘤治疗对药物暴露效应的交互修饰\",\n          \"development\": \"结合 P0537 数据，阐明近期化疗造成的急性免疫/菌群扰动可覆盖 PPI 的长期负面影响，说明治疗时序（化疗内 vs 化疗外）是解析药物 - 菌群互作的关键分层变量。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0537\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供既往化疗显著削弱 PPI 负面效应的数据，证明近期抗肿瘤治疗造成的急性扰动覆盖了长期药物暴露的影响。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U01_P03\",\n          \"point\": \"治疗阶段（新辅助/晚期）对微生物 - 疗效关联强度的修饰\",\n          \"development\": \"引用 P0593 DIET 试验在新辅助/不可切除队列中的 EFS 改善信号，指出疾病负荷与治疗目标差异导致微生物干预的表型输出不同，强化“情境绑定”论点。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供新辅助/不可切除队列中饮食干预改善 EFS 的信号，印证治疗阶段对微生物 - 疗效关联强度的修饰作用。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"unit_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U02\",\n      \"focus\": \"抗生素与 PPI 对 ICI 疗效的负面影响高度依赖使用时窗与抗菌谱类别，而非单纯的广谱暴露；特定类别表现出显著的类别特异性风险，而其他类别在调整后未见显著损害。\",\n      \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U02_P01\",\n          \"point\": \"围治疗期暴露的时间窗口脆弱性\",\n          \"development\": \"整合 P0596 与 P0606 数据，阐明 ICI 启动前后 30-60 天为菌群扰动最敏感的脆弱窗口，此时抗生素暴露对 OS/PFS 的负面影响最强，支持“维持早期免疫致敏期菌群完整性”的临床假设。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0596\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供围治疗期（尤其 ICI 启动后 60 天内）暴露风险最高的数据，支持时间窗口脆弱性假设。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0606\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"量化抗生素暴露时间窗对 ICI 生存的影响，证实术后早期暴露显著增加死亡风险，而术前暴露无显著长期影响。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0575\",\n              \"role\": \"例证\",\n              \"use\": \"利用大样本回顾性队列数据，进一步量化术后早期（ICI 启动后 60 天）暴露显著增加死亡风险（HR 1.27），细化窗口期管理策略。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U02_P02\",\n          \"point\": \"抗菌谱类别特异性风险差异\",\n          \"development\": \"对比万古霉素/PTZ 的显著负面效应与甲硝唑/部分β-内酰胺类的中性结果，论证抗菌谱广度与靶菌群决定扰动程度，挑战“所有抗生素同等有害”的简化观点。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0596\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供不同抗生素类别（如万古霉素 vs 甲硝唑）对 ICI 疗效差异化影响的数据，支持类别特异性风险论点。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0606\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"显示特定广谱抗生素（如 PTZ）在 NSCLC 中的负面效应，补充类别特异性证据。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0035\",\n              \"role\": \"例证\",\n              \"use\": \"补充代谢类药物（二甲双胍）与抗生素在 ICI 启动前特定时间窗的负面效应，揭示不同药物类别暴露时机的脆弱性差异。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U02_P03\",\n          \"point\": \"阴性队列对类别特异性的边界限定\",\n          \"development\": \"引入 P0597 HL 队列的阴性结果，说明在血液肿瘤或高强度挽救治疗背景下，抗生素类别效应可能被治疗信号掩盖，强调肿瘤类型与治疗方案对药物 - 菌群互作的修饰边界。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0597\",\n              \"role\": \"局限\",\n              \"use\": \"提供血液肿瘤队列中抗生素未影响 ICI 疗效的阴性结果，界定类别特异性效应的适用边界。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"table_tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"table_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U02_T01\",\n          \"purpose\": \"比较不同研究中抗生素暴露时间窗与类别对 ICI 疗效的具体影响差异\",\n          \"columns\": [\n            \"研究来源\",\n            \"人群/癌种\",\n            \"关注抗生素类别\",\n            \"关键时间窗口\",\n            \"对 ICI 疗效影响（HR/显著性）\"\n          ],\n          \"row_tasks\": [\n            {\n              \"content\": \"P0596：IV 期黑色素瘤，万古霉素 vs 其他，围治疗期\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0596\",\n                  \"role\": \"比较\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供万古霉素在黑色素瘤中显著负面效应的具体数据行。\"\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"content\": \"P0606:NSCLC/RCC，广谱（PTZ）vs 其他，术后早期\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0606\",\n                  \"role\": \"比较\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供广谱抗生素在 NSCLC/RCC 中增加死亡风险的具体数据行。\"\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"content\": \"P0575：泛癌种队列，术后早期暴露量化\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0575\",\n                  \"role\": \"比较\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供术后 60 天内暴露 HR 1.27 的量化数据行。\"\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            {\n              \"content\": \"P0035：mUC，抗生素与二甲双胍时机对比\",\n              \"source_uses\": [\n                {\n                  \"source_handle\": \"P0035\",\n                  \"role\": \"比较\",\n                  \"use\": \"提供尿路上皮癌中不同药物类别暴露时机脆弱性差异的数据行。\"\n                }\n              ]\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"unit_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U03\",\n      \"focus\": \"宿主生理与生活方式特征（饮食结构、年龄、地理/种族背景）通过重塑基线菌群结构与代谢输出，系统性改变微生物标志物的预测效力与方向，导致跨人群生物标志物复现失败。\",\n      \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U03_P01\",\n          \"point\": \"饮食模式对特定菌群与代谢物的定向重塑\",\n          \"development\": \"结合 P0155 与 P0484，阐明高纤维饮食通过增加 SCFA 生成与降低循环单核细胞改善 ICI 疗效，而商业益生菌可能因定植失败或菌株不匹配产生中性效应，强调饮食干预的菌株/剂量特异性。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0155\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供高纤维饮食通过增加 SCFA 生成改善 ICI 疗效的 NSCLC 队列证据。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0484\",\n              \"role\": \"背景\",\n              \"use\": \"提供衰老微生物组与饮食干预对免疫治疗反应影响的综述性框架，支持饮食 - 菌群 - 疗效路径。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U03_P02\",\n          \"point\": \"地理/种族异质性与标志物泛化边界\",\n          \"development\": \"引用 P0394 地域匹配研究，指出直接跨区移植微生物签名会导致预测精度骤降，必须通过本地化校准或地理匹配算法恢复效力，警示单一队列结论的外推风险。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0394\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供地域匹配算法恢复预测精度的数据，证明地理/种族背景导致的基线菌群异质性。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U03_P03\",\n          \"point\": \"年龄相关菌群衰老对 ICI 响应的修饰\",\n          \"development\": \"综合领域共识（参考 P0484 等背景），说明老年患者基线菌群多样性下降与特定代谢物改变可能独立于饮食/药物影响 ICI 疗效，提示年龄应作为分层分析的强制协变量。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0484\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供老年人群微生物组变化与 ICI 反应关联的综述证据，支持年龄作为分层协变量。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0155\",\n              \"role\": \"背景\",\n              \"use\": \"补充饮食与年龄交互影响 ICI 预后的观察性数据。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0181\",\n              \"role\": \"例证\",\n              \"use\": \"提供老年人群特异性“衰老富集肠型”增强 ICI 响应的实证，论证年龄相关菌群重塑可逆转传统免疫衰老预期。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"unit_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U04\",\n      \"focus\": \"肿瘤类型、分子亚型与原发解剖部位决定了肠道微生物效应的可及性与方向，部分“冷”肿瘤或强免疫抑制微环境中，单纯微生物组调节不足以逆转耐药，需结合肿瘤内在特征综合评估。\",\n      \"paragraph_tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U04_P01\",\n          \"point\": \"肿瘤免疫原性基线与微生物信号的方向一致性\",\n          \"development\": \"对比 P0585 NSCLC 中产丁酸菌的正向信号与 P0270 mCRPC 中 Akkermansia 的负向信号，论证高免疫原性肿瘤（NSCLC）与低免疫原性/内分泌依赖肿瘤（mCRPC）中同一菌属的免疫调节方向可能截然相反。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供 NSCLC 中产丁酸菌与特定预后方向相关的证据，作为高免疫原性肿瘤的代表。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0270\",\n              \"role\": \"比较\",\n              \"use\": \"提供 mCRPC 中 Akkermansia 与疗效负相关的证据，颠覆其在其他癌种中的正向预测地位，支持肿瘤类型决定方向论点。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U04_P02\",\n          \"point\": \"强抑制性微环境（肝硬化/PDAC）对微生物标志物的屏蔽效应\",\n          \"development\": \"结合 P0301 HCC 数据，阐明肝硬化背景下的严重菌群失调与强免疫抑制 TME 可使常规微生物标志物失效，提示在“冷”肿瘤中需优先解除微环境抑制屏障，微生物组调节仅能作为协同手段。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0301\",\n              \"role\": \"主论据\",\n              \"use\": \"提供 HCC 背景下肝硬化导致常规微生物标志物失效的阴性证据，说明强抑制性微环境的屏蔽效应。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"paragraph_id\": \"Ch4_Context_U04_P03\",\n          \"point\": \"分子亚型与驱动基因对微生物效应的最终过滤\",\n          \"development\": \"综合领域共识，指出 MSI-H/MSS、STK11/KRAS 突变等分子特征通过重塑抗原呈递与代谢景观，决定肠道菌群信号能否有效转化为抗肿瘤 T 细胞浸润，强调肿瘤内在生物学是微生物外周效应的最终决定层。\",\n          \"source_uses\": [\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n              \"role\": \"背景\",\n              \"use\": \"提供 NSCLC 中分子特征与微生物组关联的附属分析数据，支持分子亚型过滤论点。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0270\",\n              \"role\": \"背景\",\n              \"use\": \"提供既往内分泌治疗史重塑微生物组反应的证据，支持治疗史作为内在过滤变量。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0301\",\n              \"role\": \"背景\",\n              \"use\": \"提供 HCC 病毒背景与菌群特征脱钩的证据，支持肿瘤病因学作为过滤变量。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0205\",\n              \"role\": \"例证\",\n              \"use\": \"揭示 EGFR 突变 NSCLC 中典型有益菌预测效力缺失及独特响应菌群特征，论证驱动基因突变作为肿瘤内在过滤器对肠道菌群 - 免疫互作的修饰边界。\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants me to act as a **Chapter Editor** for a review article chapter (Ch4_Context).\nMy task is to organize the writing tasks for this chapter based on the provided input data.\nI need to:\n1.  **Assign all selected sources** (`sources`) to specific paragraph tasks or table tasks.\n2.  **Organize case-level sources** (those with `current_uses` kind=case) into paragraphs or tables, specifying their role and use.\n3.  **Define paragraph tasks** clearly: `point`, `development`, and `source_uses` (role + use).\n4.  **Reference existing paragraph tasks** (`existing_paragraph_tasks`) using their `paragraph_id`. I must not rewrite the scientific content of these tasks but can add source assignments and sequencing.\n5.  **Create tables** only if there is genuine comparative value.\n6.  **Ensure every source handle** from the input `sources` list appears in either a `source_uses` list (in a paragraph or table) or in `unused_sources` with a specific reason.\n7.  **Output a single JSON object** following the specified schema.\n\n**Input Analysis:**\n\n*   **Chapter ID:** Ch4_Context\n*   **Units:** 4 units (U01, U02, U03, U04).\n*   **Existing Paragraph Tasks:**\n    *   U01: P01 (P0585), P02 (P0537), P03 (P0593)\n    *   U02: P01 (P0596, P0606), P02 (P0596, P0606), P03 (P0597)\n    *   U03: P01 (P0155, P0484), P02 (P0394), P03 (P0155, P0484)\n    *   U04: P01 (P0585, P0270), P02 (P0301), P03 (P0585, P0270, P0301)\n*   **Sources List (14 sources):**\n    *   P0035 (case, U02)\n    *   P0053 (case, U01)\n    *   P0155 (paragraph, U03 P01, P03)\n    *   P0181 (case, U03)\n    *   P0205 (case, U04)\n    *   P0270 (paragraph, U04 P01, P03)\n    *   P0301 (paragraph, U04 P02, P03)\n    *   P0394 (paragraph, U03 P02)\n    *   P0484 (paragraph, U03 P01, P03)\n    *   P0537 (paragraph, U01 P02)\n    *   P0575 (case, U02)\n    *   P0585 (paragraph, U01 P01, U04 P01, P03)\n    *   P0593 (paragraph, U01 P03)\n    *   P0596 (paragraph, U02 P01, P02)\n    *   P0597 (paragraph, U02 P03)\n    *   P0606 (paragraph, U02 P01, P02)\n    *   *Wait, counting sources in the input list:*\n        1. P0035\n        2. P0053\n        3. P0155\n        4. P0181\n        5. P0205\n        6. P0270\n        7. P0301\n        8. P0394\n        9. P0484\n        10. P0537\n        11. P0575\n        12. P0585\n        13. P0593\n        14. P0596\n        15. P0597\n        16. P0606\n    *   *Correction:* There are 16 sources in the `sources` array provided in the input JSON. I need to make sure all 16 are accounted for.\n\n*   **Case Level Uses:**\n    *   P0035 (U02)\n    *   P0053 (U01)\n    *   P0181 (U03)\n    *   P0205 (U04)\n    *   P0575 (U02)\n    *   These need to be integrated into the paragraph tasks of their respective units.\n\n*   **Existing Paragraph Tasks Mapping:**\n    *   U01_P01: P0585\n    *   U01_P02: P0537\n    *   U01_P03: P0593\n    *   U02_P01: P0596, P0606\n    *   U02_P02: P0596, P0606\n    *   U02_P03: P0597\n    *   U03_P01: P0155, P0484\n    *   U03_P02: P0394\n    *   U03_P03: P0155, P0484\n    *   U04_P01: P0585, P0270\n    *   U04_P02: P0301\n    *   U04_P03: P0585, P0270, P0301\n\n*   **Integration Plan:**\n    *   **U01:**\n        *   P01: Keep P0585. Add P0053 (case) here? P0053 purpose: \"chemo-combined dual checkpoint... covers baseline microbiome diversity\". Fits well with P01 (chemo-immuno vs dual).\n        *   P02: Keep P0537.\n        *   P03: Keep P0593.\n    *   **U02:**\n        *   P01: Keep P0596, P0606. Add P0575 (case) here? P0575 purpose: \"quantify antibiotic exposure timing... post-ICI 60 days\". Fits P01 (timing window).\n        *   P02: Keep P0596, P0606. Add P0035 (case) here? P0035 purpose: \"metabolic drugs (metformin) & antibiotic... timing\". Fits P02 (category/timing specifics).\n        *   P03: Keep P0597.\n    *   **U03:**\n        *   P01: Keep P0155, P0484. Add P0181 (case)? P0181 purpose: \"older individuals enterotype\". Fits P03 (age) better, but P01 is diet. Let's check P03.\n        *   P02: Keep P0394.\n        *   P03: Keep P0155, P0484. Add P0181 (case) here. P0181 is about age/enterotype. P03 is about age. Perfect fit.\n    *   **U04:**\n        *   P01: Keep P0585, P0270. Add P0205 (case)? P0205 purpose: \"EGFR-mutated NSCLC... unique response flora\". Fits P01 (tumor type/subtype direction).\n        *   P02: Keep P0301.\n        *   P03: Keep P0585, P0270, P0301. P0205 could also fit here (molecular subtype filter). But P01 is about direction consistency. P0205 shows *lack* of typical benefit in EGFR-mutated. This fits P01 (direction consistency/type specificity) or P03 (molecular filter). Let's put P0205 in P01 to support the \"tumor type/subtype determines direction\" point alongside P0270. Or P03. P03 is \"molecular subtype... final filter\". P0205 is specifically about EGFR mutation. P03 seems more appropriate for \"molecular subtype\". Let's assign P0205 to U04_P03. Wait, P01 compares NSCLC (P0585) vs mCRPC (P0270). P0205 is EGFR-mutated NSCLC. It adds nuance to NSCLC. Let's put it in P03 as it's about molecular subtype filtering.\n        *   Actually, looking at P0205 purpose: \"driver gene mutation as tumor intrinsic filter\". This matches U04_P03 point: \"Molecular subtype & driver genes... final filter\". So P0205 -> U04_P03.\n\n*   **Verification of Source Coverage:**\n    *   P0035 -> U02_P02\n    *   P0053 -> U01_P01\n    *   P0155 -> U03_P01, U03_P03\n    *   P0181 -> U03_P03\n    *   P0205 -> U04_P03\n    *   P0270 -> U04_P01, U04_P03\n    *   P0301 -> U04_P02, U04_P03\n    *   P0394 -> U03_P02\n    *   P0484 -> U03_P01, U03_P03\n    *   P0537 -> U01_P02\n    *   P0575 -> U02_P01\n    *   P0585 -> U01_P01, U04_P01, U04_P03\n    *   P0593 -> U01_P03\n    *   P0596 -> U02_P01, U02_P02\n    *   P0597 -> U02_P03\n    *   P0606 -> U02_P01, U02_P02\n\n    All 16 sources are assigned.\n\n*   **Paragraph Task Construction:**\n    *   I need to use the `paragraph_id` from `existing_paragraph_tasks`.\n    *   I need to add `source_uses` to each task.\n    *   I should not rewrite `point` or `development` if I can avoid it, but the schema requires `point` and `development` in the output. The instructions say: \"`point`/`development` 可以省略——程序会把负责人原文回填\". However, the output contract shows them as required fields in the example. Wait, the instruction says \"Output Contract (only return one JSON object)\" and shows `point` and `development` in the example. But the \"Paragraph Task Reference Contract\" says \"`point`/`development` 可以省略\". I will include them to be safe and ensure clarity for the writer, copying the essence from `existing_paragraph_tasks` but ensuring `source_uses` are detailed. Actually, the instruction says \"引用负责人原任务，不重写研究内容... `point`/`development` 可省略，程序会回填负责人原文\". I will omit them to follow the specific instruction about not rewriting, but the JSON schema example includes them. To be safe and compliant with the \"Output Contract\" which shows the structure, I will include them but keep them close to the original `existing_paragraph_tasks` content. Wait, looking closely at instruction 4: \"每个段落任务写清：作者要表达的判断（`point`）、展开逻辑（`development`）...\". And instruction 4 in the second block: \"`point`/`development` 可以省略——程序会把负责人原文回填\". I will follow the second block (more specific to this step) and omit them if possible, BUT the JSON schema provided in the \"Output Contract\" section *requires* them in the example structure. To avoid validation errors, I will include them, deriving them from the `existing_paragraph_tasks` provided in the input.\n    *   Wait, the instruction says \"Output Contract (only return one JSON object)\" and shows the schema. I must follow the schema. I will fill `point` and `development` based on the `existing_paragraph_tasks` provided in the input to ensure the writer knows what to write.\n\n*   **Table Tasks:**\n    *   Are there genuine comparative values?\n    *   U02 (Antibiotics): P0596, P0606, P0035, P0575 compare timing and categories. A table comparing Antibiotic Classes & Timing Windows could be useful.\n    *   Columns: Study, Population, Antibiotic Class, Timing Window, Effect on ICI (HR/Significance).\n    *   Rows: P0596, P0606, P0575, P0035.\n    *   This adds value by summarizing the heterogeneity in findings regarding specific classes and timing.\n    *   Let's create `Ch4_Context_U02_T01`.\n\n*   **Unused Sources:**\n    *   All sources are assigned. `unused_sources` should be empty or omitted.\n\n*   **Refining Source Uses:**\n    *   For each source in a paragraph, I need to specify `role` and `use`.\n    *   `role`: 主论据 (Main Argument), 背景 (Background), 例证 (Example), 比较 (Comparison), 局限 (Limitation), 发展 (Development).\n    *   `use`: Specific description of what the source does in this paragraph.\n\n*   **Checking Constraints:**\n    *   \"Do not generate DOI, author, year or bibliographic info\".\n    *   \"Every source_handle must appear\".\n    *   \"Do not rewrite research content\".\n    *   \"Output only JSON\".\n\n*   **Drafting the JSON:**\n    *   Iterate through Units.\n    *   For each Unit, iterate through `existing_paragraph_tasks`.\n    *   Add `source_uses` to each.\n    *   Integrate `case_level_uses` into the relevant paragraphs.\n    *   Add Table Task for U02.\n    *   Ensure `chapter_argument` is summarized from `thesis`.\n\n*   **Specific Assignments:**\n    *   **U01_P01**: P0585 (Main), P0053 (Example/Support). P0053 supports chemo-combo modulating diversity signal.\n    *   **U01_P02**: P0537 (Main).\n    *   **U01_P03**: P0593 (Main).\n    *   **U02_P01**: P0596 (Main), P0606 (Main), P0575 (Support/Quantification).\n    *   **U02_P02**: P0596 (Main), P0606 (Main), P0035 (Support/Other drugs).\n    *   **U02_P03**: P0597 (Main/Limitation).\n    *   **U03_P01**: P0155 (Main), P0484 (Support).\n    *   **U03_P02**: P0394 (Main).\n    *   **U03_P03**: P0155 (Support), P0484 (Main), P0181 (Example/Age).\n    *   **U04_P01**: P0585 (Main), P0270 (Comparis